#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:55
msgid "Scan the engineer's feedback for mode signals:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:57
msgid "**Reject signals** — if ANY of these appear, use reject mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:58
msgid "\"wrong\", \"incorrect\", \"not correct\", \"off base\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:59
msgid "\"re-diagnose\", \"start over\", \"start fresh\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:60
msgid "\"this isn't it\", \"missed the mark\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:61
msgid "Explicit `--reject` flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:63
msgid "**Layer signals** — everything else defaults to layer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:64
msgid "\"also consider\", \"what about\", \"I think it might also be\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:65
msgid "\"have you looked at\", \"related to\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:66
msgid "\"in addition to\", \"another possibility\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:68
msgid ""
"When ambiguous, default to layer — it's safer because nothing is "
"discarded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:70
msgid "Layer mode protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:72
msgid "The `debug-investigator` receives:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:74
msgid "The full existing spec (including current Root Cause and Fix Plan)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:75
msgid "The engineer's feedback as additional context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:76
#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:104
msgid "These instructions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:78
msgid ""
"Treat the existing analysis as valid evidence. The engineer has added a "
"new hypothesis or thread. Investigate both the original root cause AND "
"the new hypothesis. Produce a single merged analysis — not two competing "
"explanations. If the new hypothesis supersedes the original, say so "
"explicitly. If they're complementary (e.g. a root cause and a "
"contributing factor), explain the relationship."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:85
msgid ""
"The investigator updates the spec's Root Cause and Fix Plan sections in "
"place, then appends a new round to Investigation History."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:88
msgid "Reject mode protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:90
msgid "Before the `debug-investigator` runs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:92
msgid ""
"**Archive** the current `## Root Cause`, `## Fix Plan`, and any `## "
"Investigation` sections into `## Investigation History` as the previous "
"round. Mark them clearly as superseded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:95
msgid ""
"**Clear** the Root Cause and Fix Plan sections (replace with placeholders"
" for the investigator to fill)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:98
msgid "The `debug-investigator` then receives:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:100
msgid "The spec with cleared Root Cause / Fix Plan sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:101
msgid ""
"The full Investigation History (so it can reference — but not assume the "
"correctness of — previous findings)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:103
msgid "The engineer's feedback as the starting hypothesis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:106
msgid ""
"The previous analysis has been rejected by the engineer. Their feedback "
"is your starting hypothesis. You may reference the archived findings in "
"Investigation History as evidence, but do not assume they are correct. "
"Start your investigation from the engineer's hypothesis and follow the "
"evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:112
msgid "What this skill does NOT do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:114
msgid "Does not auto-accept or auto-reject diagnoses — the engineer decides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:115
msgid "Does not delete previous analysis — layers merge, rejects archive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:116
msgid "Does not require the original session — the spec on disk is the input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:117
msgid ""
"Does not modify the debug-investigator's core investigation logic — only "
"the input framing changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/challenge-diagnosis/SKILL.md:119
msgid "Does not add Go code — this is instructions in markdown"
msgstr ""

